<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ie5fbc7b45b9b0a37e6b4584a48fbcbaf35a3e05d" commit="01b134519fb12afab2dd9994017cfde09444bc5f" commit_message="hwid: Rewrites `database.py` and its unittest.  This CL rewrites `database.py` so that it only focuses on loading/saving/manipulating a HWID database and has a well-defined interfaces for other module to access the database.  This CL also adds completely documents about the format of a HWID database file as comments in `database.py`.  TEST=make test BUG=chromium:689944 CQ-DEPEND=CL:*546098,CL:*546094  Change-Id: Ie5fbc7b45b9b0a37e6b4584a48fbcbaf35a3e05d Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/866614 Commit-Ready: Yong Hong &lt;yhong@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yong Hong &lt;yhong@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="866614" owner_email="yhong@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="12" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/14/866614/12" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2e79298ff49b304b9c17be1dfa21e95ec8c12232" commit="071423435e080eb039fc526edef300424ddb5526" commit_message="hwid: Rewrites `DatabaseBuilder` class and its unittest.  In previous CLs we implemented method for manipulating a HWID database object in `Database` class and we also removed some complex logics such as &quot;probeable&quot; from the database.  It's time to rewrite the builder for the database in a simpler way.  This CL also moves the probing related functions from `hwid_utils` module into a individual module to focus on &quot;how to use the probe tool to know what components are installed on the device&quot;.  TEST=make test; manually test all functions of hwid tools on DUT BUG=chromium:689944 CQ-DEPEND=CL:*553738,CL:*553758  Change-Id: I2e79298ff49b304b9c17be1dfa21e95ec8c12232 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/885343 Commit-Ready: Yong Hong &lt;yhong@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Yong Hong &lt;yhong@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Cheng-Han Yang &lt;chenghan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="885343" owner_email="yhong@google.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="18" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/43/885343/18" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I209ed82bcd741a25a0c3d31b7c814b6ff26879be" commit="0cd2ead49d2b2d975265a25d2995d46d14fa8893" commit_message="libcontainer/run_oci: Use rlim_t to store resource limits  This change uses rlim_t to store resource limits in both run_oci and libcontainer, since minijail has also changed the type used.  BUG=None TEST=FEATURES=&quot;test&quot;  emerge-${BOARD} \      chromeos-base/libcontainer chromeos-base/run_oci CQ-DEPEND=CL:893645  Change-Id: I209ed82bcd741a25a0c3d31b7c814b6ff26879be Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/893529 Commit-Ready: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Luis Hector Chavez &lt;lhchavez@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Yusuke Sato &lt;yusukes@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="893529" owner_email="lhchavez@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/platform2" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform2" ref="refs/changes/29/893529/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I7c44f748a6776807e59183624102eddaa15ea388" commit="c48902d26e9ded4e8b0450cae3bf84d939129293" commit_message="images: Update Chrome logo to increase resolution and circularity  The current Chrome logo (uploaded in CL:331831) is slightly oval for some unclear reason. This patch replaces it with the image currently used for the boot splash screen which is presumably officially sanctioned. As an added bonus, this logo is not only much rounder but 